  "body": "The spec talks about scrollRestoration setting affecting to the current entry.\nIf window.history object from domain A is stored somewhere and then browsing context loads\na page from domain B, the history object from domain A can affect to the scrolling restoration of the page\nfrom domain B by setting .scrollRestoration.\n\nGetting scrollRestoration has similar issue. It returns the value from the current entry in session history, which may have nothing to do with the domain in which the used history object is created.\n\n@majido\n",
